# RLS (Row-Level Security) Patterns

## Every tenant-scoped table
- ALTER TABLE public.[name] ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
- tenant_id column: uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES public.tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
- CREATE INDEX idx_[name]_tenant_id ON public.[name] (tenant_id);
- Composite index for time-ordered queries: (tenant_id, created_at DESC)

## Policy checklist
- SELECT policy with USING (tenant_id = (select (current_setting('request.jwt.claims', true)::jsonb -> 'app_metadata' ->> 'tenant_id')::uuid))
- INSERT policy with WITH CHECK (same predicate)
- UPDATE policy with USING and WITH CHECK (same predicate)
- DELETE policy with USING (same predicate)

## Performance
- Always wrap JWT extraction in (select ...) so it runs once per query (initplan), not per row
- Every tenant_id column must have an index — without it RLS causes full table scans
